In your current implementation, duplicate rows for "Dhurandhar" and "The Croods" were saved during the
processing of the second theatre because of Spring Data JPA's SQL flush behavior inside loops:
When Theatre 1 was processed, movieRepository.save(moviePayload) staged "The Croods" (movie_id: 2)
in memory (L1 Cache), but did not flush it to PostgreSQL immediately.
When Theatre 2 was processed, movieRepository.findByMovieName("The Croods") queried PostgreSQL directly.
Because the previous save was not yet flushed/committed to the database, the query returned Optional.empty().
Seeing an empty result, the logic triggered orElseGet(...) and created a duplicate row (movie_id: 6).



